  "body": "## What\n\nThe frontlight panel grows a grid of quick-setting tiles under its sliders, iOS-control-center style: **night mode, ghost-cleanup refresh, reading orientation, touch kill-switch, screenshot, sleep**. Each tile can be hidden — on-device via **Settings → Display → Customise Control Center**, or from the web config (one flag per tile). The frontlight row has no flag: it is what the panel is for. Rendering stays pure 1-bit, so the sheet stays sharp under partial refreshes.\n\nA second entry point joins the top-edge swipe: **a tap on the status-bar band** of the four top-level tab screens. Some panels' etched glass makes edge swipes unreliable; the tap is the dependable path there. The reader keeps its clean page (no status bar to tap).\n\n## Touch-only, enforced in three layers\n\nThe control center is for touch boards, and the gating is structural rather than assumed:\n\n1. The *Customise Control Center* row only exists when `mappedInput.hasTouch()`.\n2. Both entry points are touch gestures.\n3. `visibleTiles()` itself returns none without touch — if a future board grows a button binding to this panel, it opens as what it is on `develop` today: the slider-only sheet.\n\n`default` (X4/X3) builds carry zero behavior change.\n\n## The one dependency ported with it\n\nThe touch kill-switch tile needs somewhere to stand: `HalGPIO` gains a `touchEnabled_` gate over the touch queries (~15 lines), so a palm resting on the glass cannot turn pages while reading. Buttons are unaffected — which is also the way back out of the disabled state.\n\n## i18n\n\nTwo new keys (`STR_CUSTOMISE_CONTROL_CENTER`, `STR_TOUCH_TOGGLE`) added to English and Vietnamese; the generator backfills the other languages from English as usual. All other strings the panel uses already exist on `develop`.\n\n## Provenance & testing\n\nShipped and in daily use on the aurora fork (LilyGo T5 S3). On this branch, build-verified for `x4pro` (touch — full panel) and `default` (non-touch — unchanged). The tile grid itself has not run on x4pro hardware; the panel logic is identical to what runs daily on the T5 S3.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01AMRDM2sLYU4smqRpWH6fau",
